    "airGlobalOauthTitle": "Route official sessions through the proxy (OAuth replay)",
    "airGlobalOauthRisk": "Makes sessions whose main provider is Claude official (OAuth subscription login) go through the local proxy as well — the proxy reads the subscription OAuth token from the macOS keychain and forwards it to api.anthropic.com. Its only purpose: letting the Task sub-agents of an official session route to a cheaper provider (otherwise an official session connects directly and its sub-agents must stay on the official one). Sessions with a configured provider already always go through the local proxy (127.0.0.1); this switch only affects official subscription sessions.\n· Off (default, recommended): official sessions connect straight to Anthropic and their sub-agents cannot be routed independently. Zero risk.\n· On: ⚠️ replays the subscription OAuth token outside the official client, which may violate Anthropic's Terms of Service and carries account risk; it also shares the keychain entry with the CLI. The keychain is read-only (never refreshed), so once the token expires you must run claude once. Only enable it knowing the risk.",
